Concerning the ball and chain as a punishment...

Do they do any more than weigh a lot.  When I find a scroll of punishment etc.
I volunteer to read it (only once mind, since a heavy ball and chain are
impossible to move with with a reasonable amount of other equipment) since
if I'm low level, and have only one piece of Armour (a body suit that is),
the ball makes a powerful Hand 2 Hand weapon, killing most low level monsters
faster than a 2-H Sword, and it also makes a brilliant thrown wepon.

If I fall into a pit, throwing the ball might hurt my leg, but more often than
not I escape the trap.  If I dont want to carry the usual rubbish (ie the
compulsory 150 Orcish Daggers, and who ever uses them anyway?) and can survive
being hit on the head every so often by the ball, it is more a blessing than a
curse for me.

I may be a glutton for punishment, but the iron ball has advanced my experience
faster than any single item I know (I haven't yet used stormbringer which people
on this conference seem to think rather useful, and the ring of conflict comes
fairly useful), and have even wished for a scroll of punishment before now.

BTW. What does the ring of adornment do.  I read in a very reliable source (a
     cookie no less!) that it keeps nymphs away.  But from experience I don't
     think that that is so.  I found a +5 ring of adornment in a sink once, and
     would like to know if it would have helped my quest at all, of if it was
     just a ring so pretty it waranted a +5 grading.

